    <string name="voice_model_steps_title">Install the Hindi voice model manually</string>
    <string name="voice_model_step_1">1. Open your phone\'s Settings app.</string>
    <string name="voice_model_step_2">2. Go to System → Languages &amp; input → On-device speech recognition. (On some phones: General management → Voice input, or Settings → Apps → Speech Recognition &amp; Synthesis.)</string>
    <string name="voice_model_step_3">3. Tap Add languages (or the + button) and choose हिन्दी (Hindi – India).</string>
    <string name="voice_model_step_4">4. Stay on Wi-Fi and wait for the download to finish.</string>
    <string name="voice_model_step_5">5. Return to Anushtanam and tap \"I\'ve installed it — Check again\".</string>
    <string name="voice_model_steps_note">Exact menu names vary by phone brand. Look for \"on-device speech recognition\", \"voice input\", or \"Speech Recognition &amp; Synthesis\".</string>

